{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1551511908,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU0MTYzNjk5NDE=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3188","origin":"github"},"title":"Bring rev-save into -core","message":"This is a key command from -revolution that replaces `save`, `add`, and to some degree `remove` in -core.\n\nAs there is already a `save` in -core, I propose to perform the deprecation cycle discussed in a recent meeting:\n\n- introduce as `rev-save` in -core\n- add deprecation message to old `save` and `add` commands\n...\n- much later remove old commands and replace with new one, now without the `rev-` prefix -- and then deprecate the (then old) `rev-save`\n\nFixing this issue will allow `rev-run` to disappear completely.","files":null}]}